W20-1 follow-on — Adaptive Gaborish wider-corpus A/B with quality (2026-05-18)
==============================================================================

Encoder:        jxl-encoder (sibling workspace jxl-encoder--gaborish-wider-bench)
Date:           2026-05-18 (UTC)
Host:           AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM (water-cooled)
Parent commit:  swupzums 75784882 main@origin "feat(hdr): EX-J11 chunk 4"
W20-1 picked:   ruxstmol/0 ecd1ec3c → 1f772e5b (cherry-picked rebase onto main@origin)
Reproduce:      cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
                  --example adaptive_gaborish_wider_corpus \
                  --features "std butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop" \
                  -- --out benchmarks/adaptive_gaborish_wider_corpus_2026-05-18.tsv

Corpus
------
- 25 stratified CID22-512 validation photos (every other-stride pick from
  /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/, sorted)
- 5 stratified gb82-sc screenshots (every-other-stride pick from
  /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/gb82-sc/, sorted)

Grid (480 cells)
----------------
- distances: {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0}
- efforts:   {5, 7}
- modes:     {fixed=default, adapt=with_adaptive_gaborish(true)}
- (30 images × 4 distances × 2 efforts × 2 modes = 480 cells)

At distance ≤ 0.5 the encoder gates Gaborish off (libjxl enc_frame.cc:281,
mirrored in jxl-encoder api.rs:6718). Adaptive Gaborish is a no-op there.
All 60 d=0.5 cells are byte-identical (proves the silent gate, no quality
delta).

Measurement
-----------
- Encode through public LossyConfig path (so gates / profiles fire).
- Decode with jxl-oxide in linear sRGB (RenderingIntent::Relative).
- Butteraugli via Rust `butteraugli` crate (`butteraugli_linear`) on
  the planar linear-RGB images (metadata-immune; CLAUDE.md PNG-metadata
  rule).
- SSIM2 via Rust `fast-ssim2` crate on sRGB u8 images.

Default-on gate
---------------
Per task spec:
- Photos: bytes Δ ≤ -1.0% mean AND butteraugli Δ ≤ +2% mean AND
          no individual cell shows butteraugli Δ > +5%.
- Screenshots: bytes Δ ≤ +0.5% mean AND butteraugli Δ ≤ +2% mean.
- e5 AND e7 both must pass.

Aggregate result (`adaptive_gaborish_wider_analyze`)
----------------------------------------------------
class      effort  n     bytes_d%  bfly_d%  ssim2_d  worst_bfly_d%  verdict
photo      e5      100   -0.680    +0.150   -0.126   +11.642        FAIL
photo      e7      100   -0.606    -0.012   -0.110   +11.838        FAIL
screenshot e5      20    -0.269    +2.303   -0.060   +17.464        FAIL
screenshot e7      20    -0.645    +2.397   +0.086   +14.150        FAIL

Decision: KEEP OPT-IN (gate failed on all 4 cells)

Failure modes
-------------
- **Photos**: bytes-mean win is below the -1.0% photo threshold at both e5 (-0.68%)
  and e7 (-0.61%). Individual worst butteraugli cell (+11.84% at cid22/1418519
  d=1 e=7) violates the +5% per-cell ceiling.
- **Screenshots**: butteraugli-mean above the +2% ceiling at both e5 (+2.30%)
  and e7 (+2.40%), and worst cell (+17.46% at gb82-sc/codec_wiki d=1 e=5)
  far over the per-cell ceiling.

Top-3 byte wins (overall)
-------------------------
1. cid22/1025469 d=4 e=5: -4.69% bytes, +6.21% bfly (paid in quality)
2. cid22/6078297 d=4 e=7: -4.00% bytes, +0.00% bfly (clean win)
3. cid22/1544947 d=4 e=7: -3.46% bytes, +0.68% bfly (clean-ish win)

Top-3 butteraugli regressions (overall)
---------------------------------------
1. cid22/1418519 d=1 e=7: +11.84% bfly, -1.09% bytes (small bytes win, big
   quality loss on a smooth-textured photo)
2. cid22/1418519 d=1 e=5: +11.64% bfly, -1.40% bytes (same image at e5)
3. gb82-sc/codec_wiki d=1 e=5: +17.46% bfly, -0.55% bytes (screenshot smooth
   regions get over-quantized AC penalized by butteraugli's text-aware
   weighting)

Surprises
---------
- e5 and e7 behave **very similarly** (mean deltas within ±0.5pp on most
  cells). The W20-1 mapping fires the same way regardless of effort tier;
  effort only affects downstream rate-control loops which run *after* the
  Gaborish gate.
- d=2.0/e7 is the BEST cell for the adaptive path overall: bytes -0.67%
  AND butteraugli -0.51% (genuine win, no quality cost). All other (d,e)
  cells on photos either pay in butteraugli for the bytes win or break
  even.
- The W20-1 5-photo finding (-1.74% at d=1.0/e7) is corroborated as the
  byte direction (-0.98% on the wider set at the same cell) but the
  butteraugli regression on this cell is -0.04% mean — masked by the
  per-cell variance. Individual cells inside that mean swing by ±12% on
  butteraugli; the 5-image sample missed the photos that regress hardest
  (1418519 was not in the W20-1 set).

Honest stop
-----------
The original adaptive_gaborish_ab.rs comment ("A and B both decode
identically per the wire spec, bytes delta IS RD delta") is FALSE — the
decoded pixels differ because the decoder applies the *same* fixed
3x3 inverse blur to *different* post-Gab samples. Bytes-only A/B
overstates the value of the optimization by ignoring the quality
component. This sweep is the corrective measurement.
